Suppose that after twenty-three minutes, Rebecca has a single resistor with resistance $R$ ohms. How many possible values are there for $R$

solution:
Notice that $C F D A$ is a rhombus with side length 15 . If we consider the plane of the rhombus, by symmetry we have that $B$ and $E$ are right above and below the center of the rhombus, which we will call $O$. Let $A O=x, C O=y$, and $B O=h$. The Pythagorean theorem gives us

$$
\begin{aligned}
& x^{2}+h^{2}=A B^{2}=13^{2} \\
& y^{2}+h^{2}=B C^{2}=14^{2} \\
& x^{2}+y^{2}=A C^{2}=15^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Adding the first two equations and subtracting the third one gives us $2 h^{1}=140$, i.e. $h=\sqrt{70}$. Also note that $x=\sqrt{169-70}=3 \sqrt{11}$ and $y=\sqrt{196-70}=3 \sqrt{14}$. The area of the rhombus is thus $2 x y=18 \sqrt{11 \cdot 14}$. Thus, the area of pyramid $A B C D F$ is

$$
\frac{1}{3} \cdot 2 x y \cdot h=6 \sqrt{70 \cdot 11 \cdot 14}=84 \sqrt{55}
$$

Thus, the area of the octahedron is $168 \sqrt{55}$, giving the answer $168+55=223$.

