$$
\begin{aligned}
& 1^{2}+x^{2}+\sqrt{2} \cdot 1 \cdot x=B C^{2}=(2 \cdot B P)^{2}=2^{2} \\
& 1^{2}+y^{2}+\sqrt{2} \cdot 1 \cdot y=A B^{2}=A C^{2}=x^{2}+y^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Solving (using the fact $x>0$ ) yields $x=\frac{\sqrt{7}-1}{\sqrt{2}}$ and $y=\frac{3-\sqrt{7}}{\sqrt{2}}$. Then, $\frac{C P}{A P}=\frac{x}{y}=2+\sqrt{7}$, so $a+b=9$.

