Let $f_{n}=x_{n}^{2}-3 y_{n}^{2}$. We factor

$$
\begin{aligned}
x_{n}^{6}+2 x_{n}^{4}-9 x_{n}^{4} y_{n}^{2}-12 x_{n}^{2} y_{n}^{2}+27 x_{n}^{2} y_{n}^{4}+18 y_{n}^{4}-27 y_{n}^{6} & =\left(x_{n}^{2}-3 y_{n}^{2}\right)^{3}+2\left(x_{n}^{2}-3 y_{n}^{2}\right)^{2} \\
& =f_{n}^{3}+2 f_{n}^{2}
\end{aligned}
$$

Moreover, $f_{1}=1$, and by induction, we can prove $f_{n}=2 f_{n-1}$ for all $n \geq 2$. In particular, $f_{5}=2^{4}$, so the answer to the problem is $2^{12}+3 \cdot 2^{8}=4096+512=4608$.

