\end{aligned}
$$

so $\left(\frac{1}{9} x\right)^{2}=3+\frac{1}{9} x$ ．Since $x>0, x=\frac{9+9 \sqrt{13}}{2}$ ．（The sum converges because the partial sums are increasing and always less than this value．）Hence，the answer is $9+9+13+2=33$

