Note that

$$
\begin{aligned}
\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty}\left(\frac{n^{2}+n+3}{n^{2}+3 n+5}\right)^{n} & =\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty}\left(\frac{n^{2}+3 n+5-(2 n+2)}{n^{2}+3 n+5}\right)^{n} \\
& =\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty}\left(1-2\left(\frac{n+1}{n^{2}+3 n+5}\right)\right)^{n} \\
& =\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty}\left(1-\frac{2}{n}\right)^{n}
\end{aligned}
$$

which by a well-known identity is equal to $e^{-2}$.

